% references.bib - RefineID-Apple
%
% Citation entries for this repository. Machine-parseable BibTeX with
% two custom fields:
%
%   source_quality   normative | peer-reviewed | industry-published |
%                    observation | other
%   last_verified    YYYY-MM-DD when the URL / claim was last checked
%
% `normative` means the entry decides behaviour: when the code and the
% document disagree, the code is wrong. Everything else is context.
%
% Keys for the card and PKI documents are deliberately identical to the
% ones used by the Unix tree, so a citation means the same thing in
% either repository.
%
% Companion file `references.md` carries the annotations explaining what
% each entry supports and what it does NOT prove. New citations MUST be
% added to both files.

